We use complex numbers. With  $(ABC)$  as the unit circle. Let  $c=1$ , then  $a=d^2$  and  $b=\frac{1}{d^2}$ . So  $s=d+\frac{1}{d}-1=\frac{d^2-d+1}{d}$  and  $g=b+d=\frac{1}{d^2}+d=\frac{d^3+1}{d^2}$ . We have\begin{align*}n & =\frac{\left (\overline og-o\overline g\right )(c-b)-(o-g)\left (\overline cb-\overline bc\right )}{\left (\overline o-\overline g\right )(c-b)-(o-g)\left (\overline c-\overline b\right )} 
& =\frac{g\left (\frac{b}{c}-\frac{c}{b}\right )}{\overline g(b-c)+g\left (\frac{1}{c}-\frac{1}{b}\right )} 
& =\frac{g\frac{b^2-c^2}{bc}}{\overline g(b-c)+g\frac{b-c}{bc}} 
& =\frac{g\frac{(b+c)(b-c)}{bc}}{\overline g(b-c)+g\frac{b-c}{bc}} 
& =\frac{g(b+c)}{\overline gbc+g} 
& =\frac{\frac{d^3+1}{d^2}\left (\frac{1}{d^2}+1\right )}{\frac{\frac{1}{d^3}+1}{\frac{1}{d^2}}\frac{1}{d^2}+\frac{d^3+1}{d^2}} 
& =\frac{\frac{d^3+1}{d^2}\frac{d^2+1}{d^2}}{\frac{1}{d^3}+1+\frac{d^3+1}{d^2}} 
& =\frac{\frac{(d^3+1)(d^2+1)}{d^4}}{\frac{d^3+1}{d^3}+\frac{d^3+1}{d^2}} 
& =\frac{d^2+1}{d(d+1)},
\end{align*}so  $$ s-n=\frac{d^2-d+1}{d}-\frac{d^2+1}{d(d+1)}=\frac{d(d-1)}{d+1} $$  and  $$ a-c=d^2-1=(d+1)(d-1). $$  Therefore we get  $$ \frac{a-c}{s-n}=\frac{(d+1)^2}{d}=d+2+\frac{1}{d}=d+\overline d+2\in \mathbb{R}. $$  Done.

